## How it works

### Structure
- **Shadow DOM** (`mode: 'open'`) keeps the component's internals encapsulated.
- Three slots: `header`, `intro`, `details` — matching your usage.

### Behavior
| State | Intro | Details | Button | Icon |
|-------|-------|---------|--------|------|
| **Collapsed** | ✅ Visible (max-height ~120px) | ❌ Hidden (max-height 0) | ✅ "Expand more" | `+` |
| **Expanded** | ✅ Still visible | ✅ Visible | ❌ Hidden | `−` (rotated) |

### Key features
- **Click anywhere in the header** to toggle (via `onclick` + `tabindex`).
- **Keyboard accessible**: press Enter/Space on header.
- **CSS transitions** make smooth opening/closing animations.
- The **`+` / `−` square icon** rotates 180° when expanded.
- Header has a **bottom border** and **larger bold font**.
- The **"Expand more"** button disappears once expanded.

### Usage
```html
<x-details>
  <span slot="header">Section Title</span>
  <div slot="intro">Short summary always shown.</div>
  <div slot="details">Long content hidden until expanded.</div>
</x-details>
```

You can also bind it programmatically:
```js
const el = document.querySelector('x-details');
el.open = true;   // expands immediately
```

